From 5723e072e02062d504f2f7172da64804ec97ab36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michel Belleau <michel.belleau@malaiwah.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 14:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GG] fix(flashinfer): key persistent decode wrappers by
 captured shape (#396)

A captured CUDA graph bakes in the addresses of the plan buffers its
FlashInfer decode wrapper held at capture time. The dynamic wrapper
(use_cuda_graph=False) rebinds _paged_kv_indptr_buf /
_paged_kv_last_page_len_buf and reallocates _qo_indptr_buf on every plan,
so a graph captured around it replays against freed memory.

The persistent-wrapper gate admitted exactly one query length,
1 + num_speculative_tokens, so every other FULL-captured decode shape was
captured *and* replayed on the dynamic wrapper: the V2 speculator's
draft-decode graphs (q_len == 1, one token per request per draft step) and,
under num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size, each reduced-depth verify shape.
On a hybrid EXL3 + MTP-3 model the draft-decode replay faults with
cudaErrorIllegalAddress during warmup, before the server answers.

Record the shapes capture actually plans, keyed (num_decodes, q_len_per_req),
and admit a batch to the persistent wrapper only for a recorded shape. Capture
and replay then resolve to the same wrapper, hence the same plan buffers,
while shapes no graph replays keep the dynamic wrapper that replans per call.

Signed-off-by: Michel Belleau <michel.belleau@malaiwah.com>
